WEBVTT

NOTE Narration is displayed in the caption strip below the video by default.

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.439
Use the same fictional evidence in both adaptations.

00:00:03.439 --> 00:00:15.047
For a manager, foreground the scope and decision: a one-week fictional-case pilot, a reviewer for every draft and a practice log informing whether to continue or stop.

00:00:15.047 --> 00:00:18.916
Say that wider use and measured savings remain open.

00:00:18.916 --> 00:00:29.234
For a participant, foreground the working experience: examine the editable fictional example, correct or reject a draft and put questions in the practice log.

00:00:29.234 --> 00:00:35.252
The reviewer checks the result and the manager reviews questions before a next decision.

00:00:35.252 --> 00:00:38.262
Keep the organization's plain voice in both.

00:00:38.262 --> 00:00:44.280
Do not make the manager version more optimistic or hide uncertainty from the participant.

00:00:44.280 --> 00:00:47.290
Compare each adaptation with the base message.

00:00:47.290 --> 00:00:51.159
Scope, commitments, human control and approval status must agree.

00:00:51.159 --> 00:00:55.458
Select one adaptation to retain with the final reviewed message.
